manualExt -- computes the Ext module of two modules as the core Ext function sometimes does not work properly in the negatively graded case
*******************************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        M = manualExt(t, N, P)
  * Inputs:
      * t, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the homological degree
      * N, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, a module
      * P, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, a module
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 

Description
===========

Given two modules $N$ and $P$ over a ring $R$ and an integer $t$, this function
computes and returns ${Ext}_R^t(N,P)$.

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = S = QQ[X,T,Degrees=>{1,-1}];|
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : N = S^1/ideal(X*T-1);           |
+-------------------------------------+
|i3 : P = S^1;                        |
+-------------------------------------+
|i4 : manualExt(1, N, P)              |
|                                     |
|o4 = cokernel | XT-1 |               |
|                                     |
|                            1        |
|o4 : S-module, quotient of S         |
+-------------------------------------+
|i5 : Ext^1(N,P)                      |
|                                     |
|o5 = cokernel | XT-1 |               |
|                                     |
|                            1        |
|o5 : S-module, quotient of S         |
+-------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Ext: (Macaulay2Doc)Ext, -- compute an Ext module

Ways to use manualExt:
======================

  * "manualExt(ZZ,Module,Module)"

