reesCanonicalModule -- constructs the graded canonical module in a ring constructed via classicalReesAlgebra or extendedReesAlgebra
***********************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        M = reesCanonicalModule(S)
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, constructed with
        classicalReesAlgebra or extendedReesAlgebra
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * AmbientCanonical => ..., default value null
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, the graded canonical module
        over S

Description
===========

Computes the graded canonical modules of a ring constructed with *note
classicalReesAlgebra: classicalReesAlgebra, or *note extendedReesAlgebra:
extendedReesAlgebra, or

+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                                               |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : J = ideal(x^2,x*y,y^2);                                    |
|                                                                |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : S = classicalReesAlgebra(J);                               |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : T = extendedReesAlgebra(J);                                |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : reesCanonicalModule(S)                                     |
|                                                                |
|o5 = cokernel {1, 3} | -ly_1 ly_0  -y |                         |
|              {1, 3} | ly_2  -ly_1 x  |                         |
|                                                                |
|                            2                                   |
|o5 : S-module, quotient of S                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : reesCanonicalModule(T)                                     |
|                                                                |
|o6 = cokernel {1, 3} | bt_0 -bt_1 -y   x     0     0    -ti 0  ||
|              {1, 3} | bt_1 -bt_2 0    0     -y    x    0   ti ||
|              {0, 2} | 0    0     bt_1 -bt_2 -bt_0 bt_1 x   y  ||
|                                                                |
|                            3                                   |
|o6 : T-module, quotient of T                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+

The option AmbientCanonical is used to specify the canonical module of ambient
S.

Caveat
======

One should use this function and not other similar functions to create
canonical modules in extended Rees algebras, especially in older versions of
Macaulay2.  This is because core Macaulay2 Ext function sometimes gives the
wrong answer in rings with variables of negative degrees.  See this github
issue https://github.com/Macaulay2/M2/issues/3180

See also
========

  * *note classicalReesAlgebra: classicalReesAlgebra, -- computes the flattened
    Rees algebra
  * *note extendedReesAlgebra: extendedReesAlgebra, -- computes the flattened
    extended Rees algebra
  * *note gradedReesPiece: gradedReesPiece, -- gets a certain degree piece of
    an ideal in an (extended) Rees algebra

Ways to use reesCanonicalModule:
================================

  * "reesCanonicalModule(Ring)"

