reesModuleToIdeal -- embeds a homogeneous rank 1 module as an ideal in a Rees algebra
*************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (I,d,phi) = reesModuleToIdeal(S, M)
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, constructed with
        classicalReesAlgebra or extendedReesAlgebra
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, a homogeneous S-module
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * MTries => ..., default value 10
  * Outputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal of S isomorphic to M
        as a module
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the degree shift between the
        module and ideal
      * phi, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the map M to S^1 whose
        image is I

Description
===========

In the following example we embed the canonical module of an extended Rees
algebra and then embed it as an ideal.  Note there is a degree shift.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : J = ideal(x^2,x*y^2,y^3);                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : S = extendedReesAlgebra(J);                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : canMod = reesCanonicalModule(S)                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = cokernel {1, 3} | ly_1 -ly_2  0    -y2  x     0   -ti y |               |
|              {0, 2} | 0    0      ly_1 ly_2 -ly_0 -y  x   0 |               |
|              {1, 3} | ly_2 -yly_0 y2   0    0     -ti 0   x |               |
|                                                                             |
|                            3                                                |
|o4 : S-module, quotient of S                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : L = reesModuleToIdeal(S, canMod) --the first entry -1 of {-1,-2} refers |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = (ideal (ti, y, x), {-1, -2}, | x ti -y |)                               |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : Sequence                                                                |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|to the Rees algebra degree                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : L#2 -- the map from canMod to S                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = | x ti -y |                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|             1                                                               |
|o6 : Matrix S  <-- canMod                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The MTries option specifies how many attempts to make before giving up.

See also
========

  * *note classicalReesAlgebra: classicalReesAlgebra, -- computes the flattened
    Rees algebra
  * *note extendedReesAlgebra: extendedReesAlgebra, -- computes the flattened
    extended Rees algebra
  * *note gradedReesPiece: gradedReesPiece, -- gets a certain degree piece of
    an ideal in an (extended) Rees algebra

Ways to use reesModuleToIdeal:
==============================

  * "reesModuleToIdeal(Ring,Module)"

