testIdeal(QQ,Ideal) -- computes the test ideal of a pair
********************************************************

  * Function: *note testIdeal: (TestIdeals)testIdeal,
  * Usage: 
        J = testIdeal(t, I)
  * Inputs:
      * t, a *note rational number: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,, a rational number
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note AssumeDomain: (TestIdeals)testIdeal, => ..., default value false,
      * *note FrobeniusRootStrategy: (TestIdeals)testIdeal, => ..., default
        value Substitution,
      * *note MaxCartierIndex: (TestIdeals)testIdeal, => ..., default value 10,
      * *note QGorensteinIndex: (TestIdeals)testIdeal, => ..., default value 0,
  * Outputs:
      * J, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal, the test ideal

Description
===========

This computes the test ideal $\tau(R, I^t)$ of an ideal $I$ in a normal
quasi-Gorenstein domain $R$.  We begin with example in a regular ring.

+------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/5[x,y];           |
+------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^2, y^3);     |
|                              |
|o2 : Ideal of R               |
+------------------------------+
|i3 : testIdeal(5/6, I)        |
|                              |
|o3 = ideal (y, x)             |
|                              |
|o3 : Ideal of R               |
+------------------------------+
|i4 : testIdeal(5/6-1/25, I)   |
|                              |
|o4 = ideal 1                  |
|                              |
|o4 : Ideal of R               |
+------------------------------+
|i5 : testIdeal(2, I)          |
|                              |
|             2    3   4     3 |
|o5 = ideal (x y, x , y , x*y )|
|                              |
|o5 : Ideal of R               |
+------------------------------+

We now include an example in a singular ring.

+------------------------------------+
|i6 : R = ZZ/3[x,y,z]/ideal(x^2-y*z);|
+------------------------------------+
|i7 : I = ideal(x,y);                |
|                                    |
|o7 : Ideal of R                     |
+------------------------------------+
|i8 : testIdeal(1, I)                |
|                                    |
|o8 = ideal (y, x)                   |
|                                    |
|o8 : Ideal of R                     |
+------------------------------------+
|i9 : I2 = ideal(x,y,z);             |
|                                    |
|o9 : Ideal of R                     |
+------------------------------------+
|i10 : testIdeal(3/2,I2)             |
|                                    |
|o10 = ideal (z, y, x)               |
|                                    |
|o10 : Ideal of R                    |
+------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note testIdeal: (TestIdeals)testIdeal, -- compute a test ideal in a
    Q-Gorenstein ring
  * testModule(QQ,Ideal) (missing documentation)
  * *note testModule: (TestIdeals)testModule, -- find the parameter test module
    of a reduced ring

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note testIdeal(QQ,Ideal): testIdeal_lpQQ_cmIdeal_rp, -- computes the test
    ideal of a pair
  * "testIdeal(ZZ,Ideal)"
