torsionOrder -- computes the local torsion order of an ideal in a normal domain
*******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (m,J) = torsionOrder(n, I)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the maximum order to check
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the ideal you want to check
  * Outputs:
      * m, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the local torsion order of the
        ideal in the class group, or 0 if not found
      * J, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the reflexive hull of $I^n$

Description
===========

Given an ideal $I$ in a normal (or G1 + S2) domain, this computes the local
torsion order of the class of $I$.  In other words, this computes the smallest
integer $m$ such that $I^{m}$ is locally principal up to reflexification (that
is, $(I^{m})^{**}$ is locally principal).

This function returns a pair $(m, (I^{m})^{**})$ if such an $m$ is found.  If
no $m$ is found, this returns $(0, ideal 0)$.

+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z]/ideal(x*y+z^7);                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x,z);                                                    |
|                                                                        |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : torsionOrder(10, I) --the order should be 7                        |
|                                                                        |
|o3 = (7, ideal x)                                                       |
|                                                                        |
|o3 : Sequence                                                           |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : torsionOrder(5, I) --we only check up to 5, so this should return 0|
|                                                                        |
|o4 = (0, ideal 0)                                                       |
|                                                                        |
|o4 : Sequence                                                           |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+

As we are computing the reflexive hull, this function does not distinguish
between the ideal $I$ and the ideal made up of the height-one components of a
primary decomposition of $I$.

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = ZZ/5[a,b,c]/ideal(a*b-c^8)                 |
|                                                    |
|o5 = R                                              |
|                                                    |
|o5 : QuotientRing                                   |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : torsionOrder(10, (ideal(a,b,c))^2*(ideal(a,c)))|
|                                                    |
|o6 = (8, ideal a)                                   |
|                                                    |
|o6 : Sequence                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use torsionOrder:
=========================

  * "torsionOrder(ZZ,Ideal)"

For the programmer
==================

